# Competitive Analysis (audit2rbac & audicia):
Tools like audit2rbac and audicia are well-known in the Kubernetes security space. They ingest audit logs and output RoleBindings.

Our Differentiator: These existing tools are static generators. If a permission isn't used in the log, they drop it. They have no semantic understanding of the cluster. Guardian’s LLM reasoning layer is what sets it apart. Guardian can look at an unused permission, read the manifest, realize it belongs to a disaster-recovery or break-glass ServiceAccount, and choose not to revoke it. Furthermore, existing tools do not close the loop with health checks, auto-rollbacks, and continuous drift detection.
